ation of institutional resources, by avoiding duplication and fully leveraging existing synergies;

Improved compliance with the obligations under the CER and NIS2 Directives and the DORA Regulation;

The overall enhancement of national resilience, within a landscape defined by multidimensional, intensifying, and constantly evolving risks.

This Strategy also seeks to explore the feasibility of establishing dedicated and direct communication channels between critical entities, the ASCs and the SPC, to facilitate timely bi-directional information sharing regarding essential services provision and critical infrastructure resilience.

This also includes the activities of the Conference on the Resilience of Critical Entities (CRSC) which, under the coordination of the SPC, facilitates information sharing, proposes resilience-enhancing measures for critical entities, and fosters structured coordination among public institutions responsible for essential services and strategic infrastructure.

Ultimately, and in order to enhance the resilience of the public administration, it is vital to promote coordinated and synergistic action among the relevant ministries, with the Civil Protection D

the national system.

To this end, the SPC and the ASCs will facilitate public-private cooperation through:

The timely and bi-directional exchange of relevant information between public and private entities;

The sharing of best practices and the development of common models, guidelines and methodologies for risk analysis and mitigation;

The organisation of sector-specific and cross-sectoral stress tests;

The provision of training and technical support activities for the personnel of critical entities, subject to available resources.

Particular attention will be paid to low-probability high-impact (LPHI) events capable of exposing systemic, cross-sectoral or cross-border vulnerabilities.

In this regard, the Conference on the Resilience of Critical Entities (CRSC) serves as a permanent forum for dialogue between institutional representatives, practitioners, and experts, aimed at fostering a shared culture of resilience.

