sruptive effects of an incident.

The ASCs are tasked with identifying critical entities within their respective sectors and subsectors, incorporating the findings of the national risk assessment, to allow a much broader understanding of both systemic vulnerabilities and national risks. When identifying critical entities, the ASCs must also ensure alignment with the objectives defined by this Strategy.

The ASCs shall apply three fundamental criteria for identifying an entity as critical, without prejudice to EU legislation and with specific regard to the relevant criteria for identifying national strategic dual-use infrastructure:

whether the entity provides one or more “essential services” (i.e. services considered fundamental to vital societal functions, economic activity, health, public health and safety, or the environment);

whether the entity operates and its critical infrastructure are located, in whole or in part, on Italian territory;

whether any “incidents” (i.e. physical events that disrupt, or have the potential to disrupt, the entity’s capacity to provide one or more essential services) would have “significant disruptive effects” on the entity’s provision of any ser

